{:edb/db-before-t 1541 :edb/db-after-t 1542 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534854 50 #inst "2026-10-08T09:08:14.067Z" 13194139534854 true] [17592186184291 1020 #edb/ref 17592186315092 13194139534854 true] [17592186184291 1020 #edb/ref 17592186315113 13194139534854 true] [17592186184291 1020 #edb/ref 17592186315120 13194139534854 true] [17592186184292 1020 #edb/ref 17592186315099 13194139534854 true] [17592186184292 1020 #edb/ref 17592186315106 13194139534854 true] [17592186184292 1020 #edb/ref 17592186315127 13194139534854 true] [17592186184826 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534854 true] [17592186184826 1100 "> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nUse the first three terms of the Taylor expansion for $f(x) = \\sqrt{x}$ about $x = 9$ to approximate the value of $\\sqrt{10}$. Give your answer to $5$ decimal places." 13194139534854 false] [17592186184826 1100 "Use the first three terms of the Taylor expansion for $f(x)=\\sqrt{x}$ about $x=9$ to approximate the value of $\\sqrt{10}.$ Give your answer to $5$ decimal places." 13194139534854 true] [17592186184826 1145 "We use Taylor's formula in the form\n\n$$\nf(x)=f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a)+\\frac{{f}^{″}(a)}{2!}(x-a)^{2}+⋯,\n$$\n\nwith $a=9.$ \n\nCalculating the necessary derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ={x}^{1/2} \\\\ f(9) & =3 \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-1/2} \\\\ {f}^{′}(9) & =\\frac{1}{6} \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{-3/2} \\\\ {f}^{″}(9) & =-\\frac{1}{108}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the Taylor series is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{x} & =3+\\frac{1}{6}(x-9)+\\frac{1}{2!}(-\\frac{1}{108})(x-9)^{2}+⋯ \\\\  & =3+\\frac{1}{6}(x-9)-\\frac{1}{216}(x-9)^{2}+⋯\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute $x=10$ into the above to approximate $\\sqrt{10}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{10} & ≈3+\\frac{1}{6}(10-9)-\\frac{1}{216}(10-9)^{2} \\\\  & =3+\\frac{1}{6}-\\frac{1}{216} \\\\  & =3.162\\,04,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nto five decimal places." 13194139534854 true] [17592186315092 1017 #edb/ref 17592186315093 13194139534854 true] [17592186315092 1089 "q-126846" 13194139534854 true] [17592186315092 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534854 true] [17592186315092 1100 "Find the first four non-zero terms in the Taylor expansion of $\\frac{1}{x+2}$ about the point $x=-1.$" 13194139534854 true] [17592186315092 1113 #uuid "cb65a227-175b-5c42-aa58-2cfefad23b3f" 13194139534854 true] [17592186315092 1145 "We use Taylor's theorem in the form\n\n$$\nf(x)=f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a)+\\frac{{f}^{″}(a)}{2!}(x-a)^{2}+\\frac{{f}^{‴}(a)}{3!}(x-a)^{3}+⋯,\n$$\n\nwith $f(x)=\\frac{1}{x+2}$ and $a=-1.$ \n\nComputing the required derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{1}{x+2}=(x+2)^{-1} \\\\ f(-1) & =(-1+2)^{-1}=1 \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =-(x+2)^{-2} \\\\ {f}^{′}(-1) & =-(-1+2)^{-2}=-1 \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =2(x+2)^{-3} \\\\ {f}^{″}(-1) & =2(-1+2)^{-3}=2 \\\\ {f}^{‴}(x) & =-6(x+2)^{-4} \\\\ {f}^{‴}(-1) & =-6(-1+2)^{-4}=-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{x+2} & =1+(-1)(x+1)+\\frac{2}{2!}(x+1)^{2}+\\frac{(-6)}{3!}(x+1)^{3}+⋯ \\\\  & =1-(x+1)+(x+1)^{2}-(x+1)^{3}+⋯.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534854 true] [17592186315093 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315094 13194139534854 true] [17592186315093 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315095 13194139534854 true] [17592186315093 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315096 13194139534854 true] [17592186315093 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315097 13194139534854 true] [17592186315093 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315098 13194139534854 true] [17592186315093 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534854 true] [17592186315093 1041 "selection" 13194139534854 true] [17592186315093 1104 #edb/ref 17592186315096 13194139534854 true] [17592186315093 1110 #uuid "5e02c16f-1538-5865-b304-ecc4154e5812" 13194139534854 true] [17592186315094 1034 "\\frac{1}{x+2}=1+(x+1)^{2}+\\frac{(x+1)^{4}}{4}+\\frac{(x+1)^{6}}{6}+⋯" 13194139534854 true] [17592186315094 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534854 true] [17592186315094 1111 #uuid "4dc20135-5b7b-5eae-bfff-0f0a1960fe20" 13194139534854 true] [17592186315095 1034 "\\frac{1}{x+2}=2+(x+1)+(x+1)^{2}+(x+1)^{3}+⋯" 13194139534854 true] [17592186315095 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534854 true] [17592186315095 1111 #uuid "5742a0c4-23ba-5b1f-a23f-5b9e10b074dc" 13194139534854 true] [17592186315096 1034 "\\frac{1}{x+2}=1-(x+1)+(x+1)^{2}-(x+1)^{3}+⋯" 13194139534854 true] [17592186315096 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534854 true] [17592186315096 1111 #uuid "55ea2b50-1604-5d5c-bdbf-c518681a2d3e" 13194139534854 true] [17592186315097 1034 "\\frac{1}{x+2}=2-(x+1)^{2}+(x+1)^{4}-(x+1)^{6}+⋯" 13194139534854 true] [17592186315097 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534854 true] [17592186315097 1111 #uuid "51984cf6-87df-5419-bba7-fa0acef73b58" 13194139534854 true] [17592186315098 1034 "\\frac{1}{x+2}=1-(x+1)+\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(x+1)^{3}}{3}+⋯" 13194139534854 true] [17592186315098 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534854 true] [17592186315098 1111 #uuid "f46eaf94-cc1f-5b2a-bf1a-e3a51c7a0a36" 13194139534854 true] [17592186315099 1017 #edb/ref 17592186315100 13194139534854 true] [17592186315099 1089 "q-126875" 13194139534854 true] [17592186315099 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534854 true] [17592186315099 1100 "Use the first three non-zero terms of the Taylor expansion for $f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)$ about $x=0$ to approximate the value of $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1.5).$ Give your answer to $3$ decimal places." 13194139534854 true] [17592186315099 1113 #uuid "56b858e8-c4fa-5c2c-84ef-c3854e0367d4" 13194139534854 true] [17592186315099 1145 "We use Taylor's formula in the form\n\n$$\nf(x)=f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a)+\\frac{{f}^{″}(a)}{2!}(x-a)^{2}+⋯,\n$$\n\nwith $a=0.$ \n\nCalculating the necessary derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1) \\\\ f(0) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0+1)=0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{1}{x+1} \\\\ {f}^{′}(0) & =\\frac{1}{0+1}=1 \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =-\\frac{1}{(x+1)^{2}} \\\\ {f}^{″}(0) & =-\\frac{1}{(0+1)^{2}}=-1 \\\\ {f}^{‴}(x) & =\\frac{2}{(x+1)^{3}} \\\\ {f}^{‴}(0) & =\\frac{2}{(0+1)^{3}}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the Taylor series is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1) & =(0)+(1)(x-0)+\\frac{(-1)}{2!}(x-0)^{2}+\\frac{(2)}{3!}(x-0)^{3}+⋯ \\\\  & =x-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+⋯\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute $x=0.5$ into the above to approximate $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1.5).$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡1.5 & ≈(0.5)-\\frac{1}{2}(0.5)^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}(0.5)^{3} \\\\  & =0.417\\,,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nto three decimal places." 13194139534854 true] [17592186315100 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315101 13194139534854 true] [17592186315100 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315102 13194139534854 true] [17592186315100 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315103 13194139534854 true] [17592186315100 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315104 13194139534854 true] [17592186315100 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315105 13194139534854 true] [17592186315100 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534854 true] [17592186315100 1041 "selection" 13194139534854 true] [17592186315100 1104 #edb/ref 17592186315105 13194139534854 true] [17592186315100 1110 #uuid "4e2e4c4f-5dd7-5f99-a0fe-b40a225fa0bf" 13194139534854 true] [17592186315101 1034 "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1.5)≈0.424" 13194139534854 true] [17592186315101 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534854 true] [17592186315101 1111 #uuid "c241ca2c-bbf5-5377-99ef-435cbc377753" 13194139534854 true] [17592186315102 1034 "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1.5)≈0.421" 13194139534854 true] [17592186315102 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534854 true] [17592186315102 1111 #uuid "567f12c8-c922-5d6d-a930-99483ea9ef1c" 13194139534854 true] [17592186315103 1034 "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1.5)≈0.415" 13194139534854 true] [17592186315103 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534854 true] [17592186315103 1111 #uuid "9741e3d2-fd7b-5558-b19b-bdf48cbd60cf" 13194139534854 true] [17592186315104 1034 "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1.5)≈0.412" 13194139534854 true] [17592186315104 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534854 true] [17592186315104 1111 #uuid "2f228185-df63-5c8b-98a0-43513296937c" 13194139534854 true] [17592186315105 1034 "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1.5)≈0.417" 13194139534854 true] [17592186315105 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534854 true] [17592186315105 1111 #uuid "8e2a8e6d-716f-51cb-a80f-fd19f36cadd4" 13194139534854 true] [17592186315106 1017 #edb/ref 17592186315107 13194139534854 true] [17592186315106 1089 "q-126877" 13194139534854 true] [17592186315106 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534854 true] [17592186315106 1100 "Use the first three non-zero terms of the Taylor expansion for $f(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ about $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ to approximate the value of $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5}).$ Give your answer to $3$ decimal places." 13194139534854 true] [17592186315106 1113 #uuid "9fcccafb-96d2-5248-a5bc-581af0a17196" 13194139534854 true] [17592186315106 1145 "We use Taylor's formula in the form\n\n$$\nf(x)=f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a)+\\frac{{f}^{″}(a)}{2!}(x-a)^{2}+⋯,\n$$\n\nwith $a=\\frac{\\pi }{4}.$ \n\nCalculating the necessary derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡x \\\\ f(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=1 \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & ={sec}^{2}⁡x \\\\ {f}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & ={sec}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=2 \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =2{sec}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x \\\\ {f}^{″}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =2{sec}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the Taylor series is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =1+(2)(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})+\\frac{(4)}{2!}{(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})}^{2}+⋯ \\\\  & =1+2(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})+2{(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})}^{2}+⋯\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute $x=\\frac{\\pi }{5}$ into the above to approximate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5}).$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5}) & ≈1+2(\\frac{\\pi }{5}-\\frac{\\pi }{4})+2{(\\frac{\\pi }{5}-\\frac{\\pi }{4})}^{2} \\\\  & =1+2(-\\frac{\\pi }{20})+2{(-\\frac{\\pi }{20})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{\\pi }{10}+\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{200} \\\\  & =0.735\\,,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nto three decimal places." 13194139534854 true] [17592186315107 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315108 13194139534854 true] [17592186315107 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315109 13194139534854 true] [17592186315107 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315110 13194139534854 true] [17592186315107 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315111 13194139534854 true] [17592186315107 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315112 13194139534854 true] [17592186315107 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534854 true] [17592186315107 1041 "selection" 13194139534854 true] [17592186315107 1104 #edb/ref 17592186315109 13194139534854 true] [17592186315107 1110 #uuid "f3b40202-1b04-576e-97dc-7280df173f35" 13194139534854 true] [17592186315108 1034 "\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})≈0.739" 13194139534854 true] [17592186315108 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534854 true] [17592186315108 1111 #uuid "63eb126b-998b-5738-99d3-79c8d12d0f97" 13194139534854 true] [17592186315109 1034 "\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})≈0.735" 13194139534854 true] [17592186315109 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534854 true] [17592186315109 1111 #uuid "6e983fbc-7a3b-5d32-ba55-edc40db4982c" 13194139534854 true] [17592186315110 1034 "\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})≈0.744" 13194139534854 true] [17592186315110 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534854 true] [17592186315110 1111 #uuid "857b6e71-5737-5493-8f07-a81600361b2f" 13194139534854 true] [17592186315111 1034 "\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})≈0.746" 13194139534854 true] [17592186315111 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534854 true] [17592186315111 1111 #uuid "f402e085-7c9e-5902-84fa-aa694e9b204f" 13194139534854 true] [17592186315112 1034 "\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})≈0.732" 13194139534854 true] [17592186315112 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534854 true] [17592186315112 1111 #uuid "6ffed095-ed97-5bd4-9101-ccf3484fc367" 13194139534854 true] [175